Package: disappR
Title: Diagnose and Model Selective Disappearance and Appearance in Longitudinal Ageing Data
Version: 0.9.6
Authors@R:
    c(person("Krish", "Sanghvi", role = "aut"),
      person("Edward R.", "Ivimey-Cook", role = c("aut", "cre"),
             email = "e.ivimeycook@gmail.com",
             comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4910-0443")))
Description: A Shiny workflow for longitudinal ageing data that follows a
    visual-first diagnosis of selective disappearance and selective appearance:
    trait trajectories within ALR, lifespan and AFR bins, proxy-trait
    associations at each age, individual parametric fits, sampling and
    missingness diagnostics, ageing-function comparison and comparative mixed
    models (Models 1-10) with Gaussian, Poisson, negative binomial,
    zero-inflated (nbinom1 and nbinom2) and binomial families, fixed covariates
    and nested (up to three levels) or crossed random effects. Includes
    teaching simulations with known answers, ten published empirical examples,
    residual checks and exportable R code.
